\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Modern Edge at Scale\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Modern Edge at Scale Automation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf0 Overview\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 ModernEdgeAtScale
\f1\b0  deploys a vSphere Supervisor end to end in 
\f0\b VCF 9.x
\f1\b0 , following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2025/07/14/modernizing-your-edge-with-single-node-vsphere-supervisor-in-vmware-cloud-foundation-9-0/"}}{\fldrslt \ul single-node supervisor design guidance}}. It uses 
\f0\b VCF PowerCLI 9.0 or later
\f1\b0  plus 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  and 
\f2 supervisor.json
\f1  to drive cluster, network, storage, Supervisor, Argo CD, and Harbor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Prerequisites\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'95	
\f0\b VCF 9.x and vCenter:
\f1\b0  Running environment with vCenter available.\
\'95	
\f0\b Hosts:
\f1\b0  ESXi installed and cabled; management and required data networks reachable.\
\'95	
\f0\b Provisioning host:
\f1\b0  Can reach vCenter, ESXi, and the Supervisor management network.\
\'95	
\f0\b Datacenter:
\f1\b0  Already exists in vCenter; vLCM image is present in the Image Catalog (per 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1 ).\
\'95	
\f0\b PowerShell:
\f1\b0  7.4 or newer ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell"}}{\fldrslt \ul PowerShell}}).\
\'95	
\f0\b VCF PowerCLI:
\f1\b0  
\f2 VCF.PowerCLI
\f1  
\f0\b 9.0+
\f1\b0  on the provisioning host (enforced at startup and when a new log file is created).\
\'95	
\f0\b kubectl:
\f1\b0  Installed; see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/tools/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Kubernetes tools}}.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b VCF CLI:
\f1\b0  Installed; see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-0/building-your-cloud-applications/getting-started-with-the-tools-for-building-applications/installing-and-using-vcf-cli-v9.html"}}{\fldrslt \ul Installing and using VCF CLI v9}}.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Functions Performed by this Automation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 This automation performs the following:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Deployment (per edge site)\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 1.	
\f0\b Cluster creation and host addition
\f1\b0 : Creates a new cluster in vCenter and adds the specified host(s) to the cluster.\
2.	
\f0\b Cluster configuration
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	DRS set to Automatic\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	vLCM: image selection from the vCenter Image Catalog (by name from JSON or interactive prompt); cluster compliance check and remediation run before vSAN health checks.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 3.	
\f0\b VDS and networking
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	vSphere Distributed Switch (VDS) creation with required port groups (management, vMotion, vSAN, vSAN Witness as configured) and VMkernel interfaces. Management (vmk0) remains management-only; vMotion, vSAN, and vSAN Witness use dedicated VMkernels when configured.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	Physical NIC connectivity check before VDS creation; active/standby uplink teaming; MTU from config (default 9000 for vMotion/vSAN, 1500 for management and vSAN Witness).\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 4.	
\f0\b Storage
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	
\f0\b VMFS
\f1\b0 : Local VMFS datastore from available disk; storage policy for the edge datastore.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	
\f0\b vSAN OSA or vSAN ESA
\f1\b0 : vSAN enabled (OSA or ESA per config); disk auto-claim; vSAN witness traffic (and optional witness host); vSAN performance service and alarm checks (with optional 
\f2 -AcceptBadCheckResults
\f1  to proceed when health is red or vLCM remediation fails).\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 5.	
\f0\b vSphere Supervisor enablement
\f1\b0 : Supervisor enabled on the cluster with VM Operator, VKS, Velero, and Argo CD Operator services.\
6.	
\f0\b Argo CD instance
\f1\b0 : Argo CD instance created and configured. The script appends the cluster MoRef to the Argo CD namespace (for example 
\f2 argocd
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  
\f2 argocd-c462
\f1 ) so multiple supervisors on one vCenter stay unique. It prints the URL and temporary admin password when done.\
7.	
\f0\b Harbor instance
\f1\b0 : Harbor registry created and configured from a templated data file so many edge sites stay consistent and easier to maintain.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 At-scale and targeting\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Multiple edge sites
\f1\b0 : Deploys all clusters defined in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  sequentially, or a subset via 
\f2 -EdgeSite "site1,site2"
\f1  in the order specified.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Operational modes\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Validate only
\f1\b0  (
\f2 -ValidateOnly
\f1 ): JSON checks (including network segments) and YAML path checks only; no vCenter session and no deployment.\
\'95	
\f0\b Compute only
\f1\b0  (
\f2 -ComputeOnly
\f1 ): Cluster, hosts, storage, VDS, and vLCM through remediation; stops before Supervisor, Argo CD, and Harbor. JSON/YAML validation is limited to compute paths (supervisor.json, Argo/Harbor YAML, and 
\f2 common.contextName
\f1  are not required).\
\'95	
\f0\b Cleanup
\f1\b0  (
\f2 -CleanUp
\f1 ): Removes the chosen scope without deploying. Values: 
\f2 Supervisor
\f1 , 
\f2 Compute
\f1 , 
\f2 All
\f1 , 
\f2 ArgoCD
\f1 , 
\f2 Harbor
\f1 .\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	
\f0\b Supervisor:
\f1\b0  Disable Supervisor; compute stays.\
\'96	
\f0\b Compute:
\f1\b0  Remove VDS, storage, and cluster; fails if Supervisor is still enabled.\
\'96	
\f0\b All:
\f1\b0  Disable Supervisor, then remove compute.\
\'96	
\f0\b ArgoCD:
\f1\b0  Remove the Argo CD supervisor namespace for that cluster; script waits until it is gone.\
\'96	
\f0\b Harbor:
\f1\b0  Remove the Harbor Supervisor Service from the supervisor; script waits until it is gone.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	Typed confirmation is required unless 
\f2 -Force
\f1  is used with 
\f2 common.labenvironment
\f1  true (for example 
\f2 delete harbor for site1
\f1 ; use your cleanup scope and edge site name).\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Rollback on failure:
\f1\b0  Rollback follows the failure point (compute, Supervisor, Argo CD namespace, or Harbor service). 
\f2 -RollbackOnFailure
\f1  selects always, never, or prompt (Y/N/Always).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Helper functions\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Copy-ModernEdgeAtScaleTemplates
\f1\b0 : Copies all eight template files from the module (infrastructure.json, supervisor.json, infrastructure-config-help.json, supervisor-config-help.json, argocd-deployment.yml, ArgoCD operator YAML, Harbor data values YAML, and Harbor Supervisor Service package YAML) to your working directory.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp
\f1\b0  / 
\f0\b Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp
\f1\b0 : Display configuration reference (Key, Required, Notes) for the JSON files (List, Table, GridView, or Auto by terminal width; optional 
\f2 -Filter
\f1 ).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Installation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Manual Installation\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 1.	Download the module files from this repository\
2.	Extract to your PowerShell modules directory:\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	
\f0\b Windows
\f1\b0 : 
\f2 $env:USERPROFILE\\Documents\\PowerShell\\Modules\\ModernEdgeAtScale\\
\f1 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	
\f0\b Linux/macOS
\f1\b0 : 
\f2 ~/.local/share/powershell/Modules/ModernEdgeAtScale/
\f1 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 3.	Import the module: 
\f2 Import-Module ModernEdgeAtScale
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Quick Start\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Get Template Files\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The module includes default configuration templates. Copy them to your working directory:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 # Copy all template files to current directory\uc0\u8232 Copy-ModernEdgeAtScaleTemplates\u8232 \u8232 # Or specify a destination\u8232 Copy-ModernEdgeAtScaleTemplates -DestinationPath "./config"\u8232 \u8232 # Preview what would be copied (without actually copying)\u8232 Copy-ModernEdgeAtScaleTemplates -WhatIf\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 This will copy eight template files:\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  - Infrastructure configuration (vCenter, cluster, network, storage)\
\'95	
\f2 supervisor.json
\f1  - Supervisor cluster configuration (networks, load balancer)\
\'95	
\f2 infrastructure-config-help.json
\f1  - Key / Required / Notes reference for 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  (same data 
\f2 Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp
\f1  reads from the module; copy is for offline browsing)\
\'95	
\f2 supervisor-config-help.json
\f1  - Key / Required / Notes reference for 
\f2 supervisor.json
\f1  (same data 
\f2 Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp
\f1  reads from the module; copy is for offline browsing)\
\'95	
\f2 argocd-deployment.yml
\f1  - ArgoCD instance deployment YAML\
\'95	
\f2 1.1.0-25100889.yml
\f1  - ArgoCD operator package YAML\
\'95	
\f2 harbor-data-values-v2.14.2.yml
\f1  - Harbor supervisor service data values YAML\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f2 legacy-harbor-svs-v2.14.2+vmware.2-vks.1-25220498.yml
\f1  - Harbor Supervisor Service Carvel package (service definition)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Configure Template Files\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Edit the template files with your environment-specific values:\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b infrastructure.json
\f1\b0 : Update vCenter details, ESX host, cluster name, network settings, storage configuration\
\'95	
\f0\b supervisor.json
\f1\b0 : Configure supervisor cluster settings, network IP ranges, load balancer configuration\
\'95	
\f0\b argocd-deployment.yml
\f1\b0 : Configure ArgoCD instance settings. 
\f0\b Note:
\f1\b0  The namespace value in this file will be automatically modified during deployment to ensure uniqueness (the cluster MoRef identifier will be appended). The namespace value in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  should match the base namespace value in this file.\
\'95	
\f0\b 1.1.0-25100889.yml
\f1\b0 : Typically no changes needed (ArgoCD operator package)\
\'95	
\f0\b harbor-data-values-v2.14.2.yml
\f1\b0 : Configure Harbor registry data values for supervisor service deployment\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b legacy-harbor-svs-v2.14.2+vmware.2-vks.1-25220498.yml
\f1\b0 : Typically no changes needed (Harbor Supervisor Service package)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Need help configuring your JSON files?
\f1\b0  Use the built-in helper functions to view detailed configuration reference tables:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 # View infrastructure.json configuration reference (auto-detects best format)\uc0\u8232 Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp\u8232 \u8232 # View supervisor.json configuration reference (auto-detects best format)\u8232 Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp\u8232 \u8232 # Use list format for narrow screens\u8232 Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp -Format List\u8232 Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp -Format List\u8232 \u8232 # Use table format for wide screens (with separators for readability)\u8232 Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp -Format Table\u8232 Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp -Format Table\u8232 \u8232 # Use interactive grid view (Windows PowerShell only)\u8232 Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp -Format GridView\u8232 Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp -Format GridView\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Format Options:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Auto
\f1\b0  (default): Automatically selects the best format based on terminal width. Uses 'List' for narrow screens (< 120 characters) and 'Table' for wide screens (\uc0\u8805  120 characters).\
\'95	
\f0\b List
\f1\b0 : Displays each field on its own line. Works best for narrow screens (40-50+ characters). No column wrapping issues.\
\'95	
\f0\b Table
\f1\b0 : Displays data in a table format with horizontal separators between rows. Best for wide screens (120+ characters).\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b GridView
\f1\b0 : Opens an interactive grid view window with sorting and filtering capabilities. Works on any screen size but requires Windows PowerShell (not available in PowerShell Core on macOS/Linux).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 These functions display a reference table with 
\f0\b Key
\f1\b0 , 
\f0\b Required
\f1\b0  (Yes/No/Conditional), and 
\f0\b Notes
\f1\b0  for each configuration field.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 3. Run Deployment\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 # Deploy using default configuration files\uc0\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale\u8232 \u8232 # Validate configuration files only (no vCenter connection or deployment)\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -ValidateOnly\u8232 \u8232 # Or specify custom file paths and log level\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale `\u8232     -InfrastructureJson "./config/infrastructure.json" `\u8232     -SupervisorJson "./config/supervisor.json" `\u8232     -LogLevel INFO\u8232 \u8232 # Deploy a single site, or run cleanup (Supervisor / Compute / All / ArgoCD), or compute-only\u8232 # See the Start-ModernEdgeAtScale section below for more examples.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Module Functions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Main deployment function that automates the complete vSphere Supervisor deployment process.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Parameters:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f2 AcceptBadCheckResults
\f1  (Switch, optional) - When specified, automatically proceed when vSAN cluster health is red or when vLCM cluster compliance remediation fails (no Y/N prompts).\
\'95	
\f2 CleanUp
\f1  (String, optional) - Cleanup only; no deploy. Must be 
\f2 Supervisor
\f1 , 
\f2 Compute
\f1 , 
\f2 All
\f1 , 
\f2 ArgoCD
\f1 , or 
\f2 Harbor
\f1 . 
\f0\b Supervisor
\f1\b0  disables Supervisor only. 
\f0\b Compute
\f1\b0  removes VDS, storage, and cluster (fails if Supervisor exists). 
\f0\b All
\f1\b0  disables Supervisor then removes compute. 
\f0\b ArgoCD
\f1\b0  removes only the Argo CD supervisor namespace (polls until gone). 
\f0\b Harbor
\f1\b0  removes only the Harbor Supervisor Service (polls until gone). Confirm with a typed phrase such as 
\f2 delete harbor for site1
\f1  unless 
\f2 -Force
\f1  is used with 
\f2 common.labenvironment
\f1  true (see module help for the exact pattern).\
\'95	
\f2 ComputeOnly
\f1  (Switch, optional) - Run all pre-supervisor steps (clusters, hosts, storage, VDS, vLCM) then exit without enabling the supervisor or deploying ArgoCD.\
\'95	
\f2 EdgeSite
\f1  (String, optional) - Comma-delimited list of edge site names (e.g. 
\f2 "site1,site2"
\f1 ). Deploy only clusters whose 
\f2 edgeSite
\f1  matches one of the values, in the order listed. Omit to deploy all clusters. Only comma is allowed as separator; invalid delimiters or unknown site names cause the workflow to fail.\
\'95	
\f2 Force
\f1  (Switch, optional) - When 
\f2 common.labenvironment
\f1  is true in infrastructure JSON, bypasses the cleanup confirmation prompt when using 
\f2 -CleanUp
\f1 . Has no effect otherwise; a warning is shown if used without lab.\
\'95	
\f2 InfrastructureJson
\f1  (String, optional) - Path to infrastructure configuration JSON file. Default: 
\f2 "infrastructure.json"
\f1 .\
\'95	
\f2 LogLevel
\f1  (String, optional) - Minimum log level for console output. Valid values: 
\f2 DEBUG
\f1 , 
\f2 INFO
\f1 , 
\f2 ADVISORY
\f1 , 
\f2 WARNING
\f1 , 
\f2 EXCEPTION
\f1 , 
\f2 ERROR
\f1 . Default: 
\f2 "INFO"
\f1 .\
\'95	
\f2 RollbackOnFailure
\f1  (Boolean, optional) - When 
\f2 $true
\f1 : always rollback on failure (no prompt; for autonomous runs). When 
\f2 $false
\f1 : never rollback; leave site in current state and continue to next site if any. When omitted: prompt (Y/N/Always). Rollback scope is automatic by failure state (see 
\f0\b Rollback behavior
\f1\b0  below).\
\'95	
\f2 SaveHarborYaml
\f1  (Switch, optional) - When specified, the per-site Harbor data values YAML generated at runtime is moved to a 
\f2 HarborYaml
\f1  subdirectory under the module directory instead of being deleted after installation. 
\f0\b Warning:
\f1\b0  this file contains Harbor passwords and secrets in plain text. A 
\f2 [WARNING]
\f1  is shown whenever this switch is used. Delete the file immediately after inspecting it.\
\'95	
\f2 SupervisorJson
\f1  (String, optional) - Path to supervisor configuration JSON file. Default: 
\f2 "supervisor.json"
\f1 .\
\'95	
\f2 ValidateOnly
\f1  (Switch, optional) - Run JSON validation (shallow, deeper, network segment uniqueness) and YAML checks where applicable, then exit without connecting to vCenter or deploying. With 
\f4\b disableArgoCD
\f1\b0  / 
\f4\b disableHarbor
\f1\b0  on all clusters in scope, Argo- or Harbor-specific rules and YAML checks are skipped; use 
\f4\b -ValidateOnly -ComputeOnly
\f1\b0  to validate only compute-related JSON. Use to validate configuration files before deployment.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f2 Version
\f1  (Switch, optional) - Display module version and exit.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Rollback behavior:
\f1\b0  Scope follows where the run failed: compute or vSAN before Supervisor 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  full compute teardown; after compute but before Argo CD 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Supervisor disabled only; Argo CD issues 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  namespace removed, Supervisor kept; Harbor issues 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Harbor service removed only. 
\f2 -RollbackOnFailure
\f1  sets prompt, always, or never.\

\f0\b Examples:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 # Basic deployment with default files\uc0\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale\u8232 \u8232 # Deployment with custom configuration files\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale `\u8232     -InfrastructureJson "config/prod-infrastructure.json" `\u8232     -SupervisorJson "config/prod-supervisor.json"\u8232 \u8232 # Deployment with DEBUG logging for troubleshooting\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -LogLevel DEBUG\u8232 \u8232 # Deploy only a specific edge site (targeted deployments or troubleshooting)\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Deploy multiple edge sites in order (comma-delimited; only comma is allowed as separator)\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -EdgeSite "site1,site2"\u8232 \u8232 # Deploy specific edge site(s) with custom configuration files\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale `\u8232     -EdgeSite "site2" `\u8232     -InfrastructureJson "./config/infrastructure.json" `\u8232     -SupervisorJson "./config/supervisor.json"\u8232 \u8232 # Autonomous run: always rollback on failure without prompting\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -RollbackOnFailure $true\u8232 \u8232 # Never rollback on failure; leave site in current state and continue to next site\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -RollbackOnFailure $false\u8232 \u8232 # Compute-only: prepare clusters, hosts, storage, VDS, and vLCM; exit without enabling supervisor\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -ComputeOnly\u8232 \u8232 # Cleanup supervisor only for site1 (compute remains); you must type "delete supervisor for site1" to confirm\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp Supervisor -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Cleanup ArgoCD namespace only for site1 (supervisor and compute remain); confirm with "delete argocd for site1"\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp ArgoCD -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Cleanup Harbor Supervisor Service only for site1 (supervisor, ArgoCD, and compute remain); confirm with "delete harbor for site1"\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp Harbor -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Cleanup compute only for site1 (fails if supervisor is deployed); confirm with "delete compute for site1"\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp Compute -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Cleanup all (supervisor then compute) for all sites; confirm per site with "delete all for <edgeSite>"\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp All\u8232 \u8232 # Cleanup all with -Force when common.labenvironment is true in infrastructure.json (bypasses confirmation)\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp All -Force\u8232 \u8232 # Accept bad vSAN health or vLCM compliance (proceed without Y/N prompts)\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -AcceptBadCheckResults\u8232 \u8232 # Validate JSON and YAML only (no deployment)\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -ValidateOnly -InfrastructureJson "infrastructure.json" -SupervisorJson "supervisor.json"\u8232 \u8232 # Check module version\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -Version\u8232 \u8232 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u8232 # Harbor: pre-set environment variable secrets before running (recommended).\u8232 # Each $env: reference in harborConfiguration is resolved from these variables.\u8232 # SECRET_KEY must be exactly 16 characters (AES-128 requirement).\u8232 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u8232 $env:HARBOR_ADMIN_PASSWORD = "MyAdminPassword1"\u8232 $env:SECRET_KEY             = "MySecretKey12345"   # exactly 16 characters\u8232 $env:DATABASE_PASSWORD      = "MyDatabasePw1"\u8232 $env:CORE_SECRET_KEY        = "MyCoreSecret1"\u8232 $env:JOBSERVICE_SECRET_KEY  = "MyJobSvcSecret1"\u8232 $env:REGISTRY_SECRET_KEY    = "MyRegSecret1"\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Harbor: omit env vars to use just-in-time interactive prompting.\u8232 # Any $env: reference that is unset triggers a masked prompt at startup\u8232 # (before vCenter connection or any deployment step). The value is cached\u8232 # in the process environment for the rest of the run \'97 only prompted once.\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 # Console output when HARBOR_ADMIN_PASSWORD and SECRET_KEY are unset:\u8232 #   [INFO] harborConfiguration.harborAdminPassword references environment variable\u8232 #          "HARBOR_ADMIN_PASSWORD" which is not set.\u8232 #   Enter value for HARBOR_ADMIN_PASSWORD (input masked): ****\u8232 #   [INFO] harborConfiguration.secretKey references environment variable\u8232 #          "SECRET_KEY" which is not set.\u8232 #   Enter value for SECRET_KEY (input masked): ****************\u8232 \u8232 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u8232 # ArgoCD: roll back the ArgoCD namespace only, fix YAML, and retry.\u8232 # Supervisor and Harbor remain intact; their steps are idempotently skipped.\u8232 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp ArgoCD -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 # ... fix argocd-deployment.yml ...\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # ArgoCD: after a successful deployment the console shows the temporary password\u8232 # and the command to change it:\u8232 #   [INFO] Login as user "admin" using temporary password: vEHJgoj3wGtHQDlI\u8232 #   [INFO] To update your password run:\u8232 #          "argocd.exe account update-password --server 10.40.12.203 --account admin --insecure"\u8232 \u8232 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u8232 # Harbor: roll back Harbor only, fix configuration, and retry.\u8232 # Supervisor and ArgoCD remain intact; their steps are idempotently skipped.\u8232 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp Harbor -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 # ... fix infrastructure.json harborConfiguration ...\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Autonomous run with Harbor and ArgoCD: always rollback on failure, no prompts\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -RollbackOnFailure $true\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 EdgeSite Parameter Usage:
\f1\b0 \
The 
\f2 -EdgeSite
\f1  parameter lets you target one or more edge sites from your infrastructure.json instead of processing all clusters. Use a comma-delimited list to deploy multiple sites (e.g. 
\f2 -EdgeSite "site1,site2"
\f1 ). This is useful for the following:\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Targeted deployments
\f1\b0 : Deploy or redeploy specific edge sites without processing others\
\'95	
\f0\b Troubleshooting
\f1\b0 : Isolate issues to specific clusters\
\'95	
\f0\b Incremental rollouts
\f1\b0 : Deploy a subset of sites in a chosen order\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Testing
\f1\b0 : Validate configuration for selected sites before deploying all\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 How it works:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	When 
\f2 -EdgeSite
\f1  is 
\f0\b not specified
\f1\b0 : All clusters in the 
\f2 clusters[]
\f1  array are processed sequentially. The script connects to vCenter once and processes each cluster in order, maintaining the connection between clusters that share the same vCenter FQDN.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	When 
\f2 -EdgeSite
\f1  
\f0\b is specified
\f1\b0 : Only clusters whose 
\f2 edgeSite
\f1  matches one of the comma-separated values are processed, in the order you list them (e.g. 
\f2 -EdgeSite "site2,site1"
\f1  deploys site2 then site1).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Important Notes:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	Use 
\f0\b only a comma
\f1\b0  to separate site names. Invalid delimiters (e.g. semicolon) cause the workflow to fail.\
\'95	Each value must exactly match an 
\f2 edgeSite
\f1  in your infrastructure.json 
\f2 clusters[]
\f1  array. If any specified site is invalid, the workflow fails with the list of valid values.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	All clusters in the same infrastructure.json share the same vCenter connection (from 
\f2 common.vCenterName
\f1 ), so the connection persists when processing multiple clusters.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

