\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Configuration Files\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Deployment is driven by two JSON inputs: 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  (vCenter, clusters, networking, storage, ArgoCD paths) and 
\f2 supervisor.json
\f1  (supervisor sizing, load balancer, and network IP ranges). Each 
\f2 edgeSite
\f1  in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  
\f2 clusters[]
\f1  must have a matching 
\f2 edgeSite
\f1  in 
\f2 supervisor.json
\f1  
\f2 tkgsSiteSpec[]
\f1 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 infrastructure.json\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 This file defines vCenter connection, datacenter, and shared naming prefixes; then one or more clusters, each with ESX hosts, storage type, networking segments, and ArgoCD paths. Many fields are 
\f0\b optional
\f1\b0  and have defaults so you can omit them for a minimal config.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Structure:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f4\b common
\f1\b0  \'96 Settings used for all clusters (one vCenter, one datacenter, shared prefixes and content library). Prefixes and 
\f2 esxUser
\f1  are optional; when omitted, defaults apply (see tables below).\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f4\b clusters
\f1\b0  \'96 Array of cluster objects. Each cluster is identified by 
\f2 edgeSite
\f1  (must match a site in 
\f2 supervisor.json
\f1 ). Per-cluster you define ESX hosts, storage type, and network segments. ArgoCD YAML paths may be defined here to override the common defaults.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Important behavior:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Uplinks:
\f1\b0  There is no 
\f2 numUplinks
\f1  field. The number of VDS uplinks is taken from the length of 
\f2 nicList
\f1  (e.g. two NICs in 
\f2 nicList
\f1  means two uplinks). 
\f0\b nicList
\f1\b0  may be defined at 
\f0\b common
\f1\b0  (applies to all clusters) or per 
\f0\b clusters[]
\f1\b0  (cluster overrides common). At least one definition is mandatory: either 
\f2 common.nicList
\f1  or 
\f2 clusters[].nicList
\f1  for each cluster. When both are defined, the cluster value takes precedence. Effective list must have 2 or 4 NICs.\
\'95	
\f0\b Storage:
\f1\b0  Use 
\f2 storagePolicy.storageType
\f1  (
\f2 VMFS
\f1 , 
\f2 vSAN-ESA
\f1 , or 
\f2 vSAN-OSA
\f1 ). The tag catalog name can be omitted; it defaults to 
\f2 \{storageType\}-Storage-TagCatalog
\f1  (e.g. 
\f2 VMFS-Storage-TagCatalog
\f1 ).\
\'95	
\f0\b vSAN witness:
\f1\b0  
\f2 vSanWitnessVmName
\f1  may be defined at 
\f2 common
\f1  (applies to all vSAN clusters) or per 
\f2 clusters[]
\f1  (cluster root level only; cluster overrides common). Required for vSAN-OSA and vSAN-ESA storage types; not used for VMFS.\
\'95	
\f0\b vSphere HA admission (vSAN OSA/ESA only):
\f1\b0  
\f2 haPolicy
\f1  may be defined at 
\f2 common
\f1  or per 
\f2 clusters[]
\f1  (cluster overrides common). Omitted means 
\f4\b slotBased
\f1\b0  (host failures tolerated = 1, slot-style admission). 
\f4\b reservationBased
\f1\b0  reserves CPU and memory using cluster percentage admission (same as the previous module default for multi-host). 
\f4\b disabled
\f1\b0  leaves HA on with admission control off (VM restart only, no capacity reservation). These values apply when the workflow re-applies HA after moving management to the VDS and when the vSAN alarm check remediates 
\f0\b vSphere HA host status
\f1\b0 . 
\f0\b VMFS
\f1\b0  clusters are not governed by this JSON key; HA re-apply after the VDS step continues to use 
\f0\b reservationBased
\f1\b0  so behavior matches earlier releases. When the key is present, JSON validation accepts only the three strings above.\
\'95	
\f0\b ArgoCD YAML paths:
\f1\b0  
\f2 supervisorServices.argoCdOperatorYamlPath
\f1  and 
\f2 supervisorServices.argoCdDeploymentYamlPath
\f1  may be defined at 
\f2 common
\f1  (applies to all clusters) or per 
\f2 clusters[]
\f1  (cluster overrides common). If any cluster omits both paths, 
\f2 common.supervisorServices
\f1  must define them; if every cluster defines its own paths, 
\f2 common.supervisorServices
\f1  is not required. Cluster-level always takes priority when both levels are defined. 
\f2 supervisorServices.nameSpacePrefix
\f1  defaults to 
\f2 argocd
\f1  if omitted. 
\f2 supervisorServices.vmClass
\f1  is optional; when omitted, the script assigns all VM classes reported by vCenter to the ArgoCD namespace.\
\'95	
\f0\b Disabling supervisor services:
\f1\b0  Set 
\f2 supervisorServices.disableArgoCD: true
\f1  or 
\f2 supervisorServices.disableHarbor: true
\f1  at 
\f2 common
\f1  (affects all clusters) or per 
\f2 clusters[]
\f1  (overrides common for that cluster only). Both default to 
\f2 false
\f1  (enabled). When 
\f2 disableArgoCD
\f1  is true, the ArgoCD service, namespace, operator, and instance steps are all skipped and the ArgoCD YAML paths do not need to be configured. When 
\f2 disableHarbor
\f1  is true, Harbor service registration, data values generation, and installation are all skipped; 
\f2 harborConfiguration
\f1  is not required and 
\f2 harborServiceYamlPath
\f1  does not need to be configured.\
\'95	
\f0\b Harbor configuration:
\f1\b0  Each cluster needs a 
\f2 harborConfiguration
\f1  block unless 
\f2 disableHarbor
\f1  is true.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'96	
\f0\b Hostname:
\f1\b0  
\f2 harborConfiguration.hostname
\f1  is required (FQDN or IP that DNS accepts).\
\'96	
\f0\b Volume sizes:
\f1\b0  Optional 
\f2 registryVolumeSize
\f1 , 
\f2 jobserviceVolumeSize
\f1 , 
\f2 databaseVolumeSize
\f1 , 
\f2 redisVolumeSize
\f1 , 
\f2 trivyVolumeSize
\f1  use 
\f2 <positive integer>Gi
\f1  (for example 
\f2 10Gi
\f1 ).\
\'96	
\f0\b Secrets:
\f1\b0  Optional keys map into the Harbor data values YAML. Prefix with 
\f2 $env:VAR
\f1  to load at runtime so secrets stay out of JSON.\
\'96	
\f0\b Prompts:
\f1\b0  If 
\f2 $env:
\f1  is used and the variable is unset, the script asks once during pre-flight (masked input) and caches the value for the process. Plain text in JSON is never prompted for.\
\'96	
\f0\b TLS:
\f1\b0  
\f2 tlsCrt
\f1  and 
\f2 tlsKey
\f1  are PEM file paths and must appear together; optional 
\f2 caCrt
\f1  only when both are set. Paths are validated before deploy.\
\'96	
\f0\b Service YAML:
\f1\b0  Download the Harbor Supervisor Service Carvel package from Broadcom; set 
