\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Cleanup: Management Restore or VDS Removal Fails\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Cleanup no longer requires 
\f2 clusters.networking.temporaryManagementIp
\f1 . Management (vmk0) is moved from the VDS to a standard switch programmatically using the same API as vCenter\'92s 
\f0\b Migrate VMkernel Adapter
\f1\b0  wizard. If that fails, the script reports the error and instructs you to move vmk0 manually in vCenter, then re-run cleanup.\
If cleanup reports "could not remove any pNIC from VDS" (vSphere rolled back to avoid disconnecting the host) or "Port group mgmt is in use":\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 1.	In vCenter go to 
\f0\b Host 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Configure 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Networking 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  VMkernel adapters
\f1\b0  for each host in the cluster.\
2.	Edit 
\f0\b vmk0
\f1\b0  and change its port group from the distributed "mgmt" port group to a standard switch (e.g. create a temporary vSwitch with one pNIC and a Management port group, or use an existing standard switch).\
3.	Save so vmk0 is on a standard switch on all hosts.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 4.	Re-run cleanup with the same parameters (e.g. 
\f2 -EdgeSite site2 -CleanUp Compute -Force
\f1 ). With management off the VDS, cleanup will skip restore and remove the VDS and cluster.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Harbor: secretKey Wrong Length\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 When using 
\f4 $env:
\f0  references:
\f1\b0  The script detects a wrong-length value during the pre-flight prompting phase and asks whether you want to re-enter:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 [ERROR] Environment variable "SECRET_KEY" (harborConfiguration.secretKey) has 8 character(s)\uc0\u8232         but must be exactly 16.\u8232 Would you like to re-enter harborConfiguration.secretKey? (Y/N): Y\u8232 [WARNING] Prompting for corrected value for harborConfiguration.secretKey (env:SECRET_KEY).\u8232 Enter value for harborConfiguration.secretKey (env:SECRET_KEY): ________________\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Y
\f1\b0  \'97 re-prompts. The Y/N question repeats after each wrong-length entry.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b N
\f1\b0  \'97 aborts deployment cleanly. No rollback is needed; nothing has been deployed yet.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 When using a plain-text value in JSON:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 [ERROR] clusters[].harborConfiguration.secretKey for edgeSite "site1" must be\uc0\u8232         exactly 16 characters but is 8 character(s). Harbor uses it as an AES-128\u8232         encryption key.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Fix:
\f1\b0  Update the 
\f2 secretKey
\f1  value in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  to exactly 16 characters, then re-run. No rollback is needed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Harbor: TLS Certificate and Key Swapped (PEM Type Mismatch)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Error:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 [ERROR] clusters[].harborConfiguration.tlsCrt must contain a PEM certificate\uc0\u8232         (-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----) but the file at "...\\tls.crt" begins with\u8232         "-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----" for edgeSite "site1".\u8232         Check that tlsCrt and tlsKey paths are not swapped.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Fix:
\f1\b0  Verify that 
\f2 tlsCrt
\f1  points to the certificate file and 
\f2 tlsKey
\f1  points to the private key file. This error is caught at pre-flight validation before any deployment begins.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Harbor: Service Enters ERROR State\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 If Harbor enters an 
\f2 ERROR
\f1  state shortly after installation (within 5\'9610 seconds of the first status poll):\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 1.	
\f0\b Check vCenter Events
\f1\b0  (Menu 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Events) for messages containing 
\f2 "Registering harbor.tanzu.vmware.com... already exists"
\f1 . If present, this is a vCenter async conflict: delete the service from 
\f0\b Menu 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Supervisor Management 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Services
\f1\b0 , then roll back and re-run.\
2.	
\f0\b Check the secretKey length
\f1\b0  \'97 Harbor will fail immediately if 
\f2 secretKey
\f1  is not exactly 16 characters. Look for 
\f2 [ERROR]
\f1  messages about secretKey length in the pre-flight output.\
3.	
\f0\b Check the vCenter Events for detailed error text
\f1\b0  \'97 the 
\f2 ERROR
\f1  message from the script (e.g. 
\f2 "OCI Registry"
\f1 ) identifies the failing component but not the root cause. The full error is in vCenter Events for the supervisor.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 4.	
\f0\b Admission or scheduling:
\f1\b0  HA admission can block new VMs even when free capacity looks sufficient. For vSAN OSA/ESA, try 
\f4\b haPolicy
\f1\b0  in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  (
\f2 slotBased
\f1 , 
\f2 reservationBased
\f1 , or 
\f2 disabled
\f1 ) or change HA admission in vCenter, then retry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Recovery:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 # Roll back Harbor only (supervisor and ArgoCD remain).\uc0\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -CleanUp Harbor -EdgeSite "site1"\u8232 \u8232 # Fix the issue, then retry.\u8232 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale -EdgeSite "site1"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

