\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Execution Steps\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Install VCF.PowerCLI Module\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Install the required PowerCLI module for VCF.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Install module and copy template files\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Recommended:
\f1\b0  Install 
\f0\b ModernEdgeAtScale
\f1\b0  per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#installation"}}{\fldrslt \ul Installation}}, run 
\f2 Import-Module ModernEdgeAtScale
\f1 , then copy the bundled templates to your working directory:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 Copy-ModernEdgeAtScaleTemplates -DestinationPath "./config"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 That copies eight files (paths in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  must point to where you placed them):\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  \'96 vCenter, clusters, networks, storage, supervisor service YAML paths, Harbor settings\
\'95	
\f2 supervisor.json
\f1  \'96 Supervisor networking, load balancer, sizing\
\'95	
\f2 infrastructure-config-help.json
\f1  \'96 Reference table source for 
\f2 Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp
\f1  (offline copy alongside your JSON)\
\'95	
\f2 supervisor-config-help.json
\f1  \'96 Reference table source for 
\f2 Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp
\f1  (offline copy alongside your JSON)\
\'95	
\f2 argocd-deployment.yml
\f1  \'96 Argo CD instance CustomResource spec (often usable as-is for lab; customize for production)\
\'95	
\f2 1.1.0-25100889.yml
\f1  \'96 Argo CD operator Carvel package (usually unchanged)\
\'95	
\f2 harbor-data-values-v2.14.2.yml
\f1  \'96 Harbor registry data values (hostname, TLS, secrets)\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f2 legacy-harbor-svs-v2.14.2+vmware.2-vks.1-25220498.yml
\f1  \'96 Harbor Supervisor Service package (usually unchanged)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Alternate:
\f1\b0  If you use a zip bundle instead of the gallery module, extract it and use the same filenames (typically under 
\f2 Templates
\f1  next to the 
\f2 .psm1
\f1 ). Update paths in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  to match your machine.\
For sample JSON and 
\f2 Start-ModernEdgeAtScale
\f1  usage, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "EXAMPLE.md"}}{\fldrslt \ul EXAMPLE.md}}.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Configure infrastructure.json\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Open 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  and review all the fields, updating as required for your environment. 
\f0\b Accuracy here is crucial for successful deployment.
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	Set 
\f2 supervisorServices.argoCdOperatorYamlPath
\f1  and 
\f2 supervisorServices.argoCdDeploymentYamlPath
\f1  to your copies of the operator YAML and 
\f2 argocd-deployment.yml
\f1  unless Argo CD is disabled (
\f2 supervisorServices.disableArgoCD
\f1 ).\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	Configure Harbor template paths and 
\f2 harborConfiguration
\f1  unless Harbor is disabled (
\f2 supervisorServices.disableHarbor
\f1 ).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Argo CD namespace:
\f1\b0  The base namespace in 
\f2 argocd-deployment.yml
\f1  must match 
\f2 supervisorServices.nameSpacePrefix
\f1  (default 
\f2 argocd
\f1 ). During deployment the script appends the cluster MoRef (e.g. 
\f2 argocd
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  
\f2 argocd-c462
\f1 ) so multiple supervisors on one vCenter do not collide. Edit 
\f2 argocd-deployment.yml
\f1  only when you need a non-default instance spec; see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vsphere-supervisor-services-and-standalone-components/latest/using-supervisor-services/using-argo-cd-service/argocd-custom-resrouce-reference.html"}}{\fldrslt \ul Argo CD service documentation}}.\

