\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 5. Argo CD operator YAML (optional)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 If Broadcom publishes a newer Argo CD operator package than the template (
\f2 1.1.0-25100889.yml
\f1 ), download it from the product documentation and set 
\f2 supervisorServices.argoCdOperatorYamlPath
\f1  in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1  to that file.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 6. Install VCF CLI\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'95	Install the VCF CLI per Broadcom: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-0/building-your-cloud-applications/getting-started-with-the-tools-for-building-applications/installing-and-using-vcf-cli-v9.html"}}{\fldrslt \ul Installing and Using VCF CLI v9}}. First-run terms and CEIP are described there; set those before unattended automation.\
\'95	
\f0\b Windows:
\f1\b0  The installer typically provides 
\f2 vcf.exe
\f1 . The module accepts 
\f4\b vcf.exe
\f0  or 
\f4 vcf
\f1\b0  on PATH (it picks the first name that resolves). Rename or adjust only if your deployment standard requires a specific filename.\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Linux / macOS:
\f1\b0  Use the 
\f2 vcf
\f1  binary from the same documentation. Install 
\f0\b kubectl
\f1\b0  from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/tools/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Kubernetes install tools}} if you have not already.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Important Notes\
\pard\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'95	
\f0\b Networks:
\f1\b0  Expect the four-network edge layout (management, workload, two load balancer segments) and four VLAN IDs in 
\f2 infrastructure.json
\f1 , matching the design docs linked above.\
\'95	
\f0\b CLI tools:
\f1\b0  Install 
\f0\b kubectl
\f1\b0  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/tools/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Kubernetes install tools}}) and the 
\f0\b VCF CLI
\f1\b0  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-0/building-your-cloud-applications/getting-started-with-the-tools-for-building-applications/installing-and-using-vcf-cli-v9.html"}}{\fldrslt \ul Installing and Using VCF CLI v9}}) before you run the module (see step 6).\
\'95	
\f0\b Platforms:
\f1\b0  Tested on Windows and macOS with PowerShell 7.4+.\
}